course: dictionary
lesson: 604
title: Away: leaving, distance and time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Away is a small word with many jobs. Most often it means off, or not here any more. «If 6 of those 24 pencils are given away, 24 − 6 = 18 are left.» The pencils have left the group, so fewer are left.
explain: Away can also show distance or time. «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.» Here away means at a distance from the dog. In «the party is two weeks away», away tells you how far off the party is in time.
explain: Away can also mean on and on. «Add soap and the grease slides away.» The grease moves off the plate and is gone. Ask yourself: is something leaving, is it far off, or is it happening over time? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Away means off to another place, not here any more, as in «the bird flew away».
fact: Away means at a distance, as in «the beach is 2 km away».
fact: Away means on and on, as in «he worked away all day».
fact: «Right away» means at once, and «a takeaway» (UK, Australia, New Zealand) is food to take home.
fact: «Away with you!» in the UK and Ireland can mean «I don't believe you».
exercise: «The beach is 2 km away.» What does away tell you here? | At once | Off, gone from here | *At a distance | On and on
exercise: «He worked away all day.» What does away mean? | *On and on, without stopping | Off to another place | In the future | Not at home
exercise: «The party is two weeks away.» What does away show? | Something has left the group | A rude way to tell someone to leave | Working hard | *Time still to come, in the future
test: «The bird flew away.» Which meaning of away is this? | On and on | At a distance | *Off to another place, not here any more | In the future
test: «Counting the seconds shows whether the storm is coming closer or moving away.» What does away mean here? | Working hard all day | Going home to rest | *Getting further from you | Coming in the future
exam: Which formal exam word could replace «taken away» in «6 pencils were taken away»? | Ran | Stayed | Flew | *Removed
